      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this change moves this logic in [CheckAvailableForApex](https://cs.android.com/android/_/android/platform/build/soong/+/93c52efc1591943238c96b58e51248a71f310194:android/apex.go;l\u003d452-454;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0;drc\u003d8c9ae7ed6770b45f1337722a2e61cb22317659aa) inside ApexAvailable, I expect this to not break vendor modules. We can have an additional check in [markPlatformAvailability](https://cs.android.com/android/_/android/platform/build/soong/+/93c52efc1591943238c96b58e51248a71f310194:apex/apex.go;l\u003d1242;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0;drc\u003d95cd6db590a5be0fa822cf8741454a0874cc259a) mutator to ignore/special-case the vendor variants if necessary. Something like\n```\nif mctx.Host() || mctx.Module().InstallInRecovery() || mctx.Vendor() {\n  return\n}\n```\n\nJooyung, is there a way to actually verify this? There was no diff in the ninja files with/without this change* in aosp. Is there a postsubmit build that I can trigger to test this?\n\n(* only when run with BUILD_BROKEN_DISABLE_BAZEL\u003dtrue. Without it, there are some diffs, but I believe the updated BUILD files are the correct ones https://diff.googleplex.com/#key\u003daFrWfhs4Phn5 cc +eakammer)",
